            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked: \u201cWhat about the --\u201d."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice SOUTER",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0014"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 33,
              "start": 33
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked: \u201cWhat did Congress intend? And --\u201d."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0015"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 34,
              "start": 34
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked: \u201cAnd are you aware \u2014 you mentioned the 100 years of State precedent \u2014 is there any precedent in the State law for class actions for holder claims?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3d6d37546a34-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked: \u201cWhat is there in the statute that says the two have to go with each other?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3d6d37546a34-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked: \u201cOne is \u2014 we know about the holder claims. They are saved for State actions. They're not preempted. What else would fall in this category that is not \u2014 that SLUSA doesn't affect, that can be brought as class actions in State court?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer and Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3d6d37546a34-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer and Justice Ginsburg, justices Breyer and Ginsburg asked questions illustrating that Congress could not have intended such an anomalous result by allowing holders\u2019 claims to proceed as non\u2011preempted."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3d6d37546a34-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Mr. Frederick explained that the congressional findings in SLUSA were narrowly framed to preempt only Federal\u2011law claims, not State\u2011law holder claims."
      }
    ],
