  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 22,
                "start": 22
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, the respondent described the state of the law as accurate in theory, but noted that respondents have not been able to point to a single reported holder class\u2011action case in State court prior to the adoption of the Uniform Standards Act."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, the respondent explained that Blue Chip was not about the scope of the \u201cin connection with\u201d requirement or the \u00a710(b) prohibition; rather, it concerned what Congress would have wanted to authorize as a right of action."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0008"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The respondent\u2019s position is that SLUSA does not preempt class actions asserting holder claims because Congress incorporated the Court\u2019s interpretation of \u201cin connection with\u201d from Blue Chip Stamps when it enacted SLUSA."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0009"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 26,
                "start": 26
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The respondent asserted that SLUSA does not preempt holder claims for private civil\u2011action purposes."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0011"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 28,
                "start": 28
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, the respondent noted that the Court\u2019s decision in Blue Chip Stamps involved non\u2011purchasers, which is a very different kind of case."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0012"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 29,
                "start": 29
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The respondent argued that a holder\u2019s claim would not exist but for purchases and sales that caused the price to rise."
        }
      ],
